2026-11-06 02:25 Reproduced on HEAD (scratch script, both reactors): (1) a child that exits while something of its own still holds the socket (perl -e 'exit 5 if fork; sleep 1') reads 'exited (unknown)' under EV every time, 'exited (code 5)' under Poll -- the EV reaping race made deterministic. (2) A call that arrives while the child is being stopped (idle stop, warm-up's lazy stop) takes start_p's ready fast path, goes to the dying child and fails with 'exited (signal 15)' under BOTH reactors -- that, not EV, is why t/reload.t 'a changed entry is rebuilt' flaked (its 'after' call races the background warm-up's stop; EV only turned the text into 'unknown'). Fixing (2) too: start_p waits for a child on its way out and starts the next one, one child at a time -- which the async exit needs anyway, or a new child could be attached before the old one's exit is handled.

2026-11-06 02:46 Fix in place: MCP::Hub::Child::watch_exit (EV::child watcher at fork + WNOHANG poll once the output closed; Docker::run_p now uses it too). Upstream::Stdio: _on_close only marks the socket closed and starts collecting; _on_exit($status) does the old bookkeeping once close+status are both in (Fork/Docker::Stdio overrides moved there, Docker::Stdio takes the status as an argument instead of stashing it in _exit_hint). Per-child state lives in $self->{child} {collect, closed, reaped, status, killed, linger}. Decisions (mine): a child that closed its socket but still runs is SIGKILLed after KILL_GRACE (5s) with a warn line -- it can never answer again; a stop is bounded: after the grace it is killed, or -- reaped already while a process it started holds the socket -- the hub hangs up its socket end; start_p waits for a child on its way out (stopping / socket closed / failed start) and then starts the next, so a call during an idle stop is served instead of failing. Tests red on HEAD (run against a git-archive of HEAD lib), green now under EV and Poll: 6 subtests in t/stdio.t.

Done, commit-ready (uncommitted). Root cause: Stdio::_on_close did a blocking waitpid(pid,0) once the socket closed. Under EV, libev reaps every child via its SIGCHLD handler, so the status was lost ('exited (unknown)'). A child that closed stdout and lived on held the whole loop: 0 ticks on HEAD. The t/reload.t flake is a call racing a stop (red under EV and Poll; EV only turned the text into 'unknown'), not the k58 diagnosis. Fix: MCP::Hub::Child::watch_exit(pid, cb) puts an EV::child watcher in place right after fork, plus a WNOHANG poll every 50 ms once the output is closed. Docker::run_p uses it too, replacing its own EV/Poll branches. In Stdio, exit is two-phase: _on_close (socket) + _on_reaped (status) -> _on_exit (bookkeeping, crash-loop count, k48 fail reasons). A stop is bounded and pid-bound (TERM, then _kill_now after 5 s; hang up if already reaped while a grandchild holds the socket). A child that closes stdout and keeps running is SIGKILLed after 5 s with a warn line. start_p waits for a leaving child (_gone_p), one child at a time. Fork/Docker::Stdio now hook _on_exit. Removed local SIG{CHLD}='DEFAULT' from t/fork.t. Tightened t/hub.t / t/fork-lifecycle.t to exact statuses. 5 new t/stdio.t subtests, all red on HEAD lib. Verified: the 7 affected suites pass under EV and MOJO_REACTOR=Mojo::Reactor::Poll. prove -lr t/ PASS (Files=28 Tests=258). The k23-only tree (k56+k22 reversed) passes t/stdio.t t/hub.t t/fork.t. Split: reverse-apply scratchpad w-k23/k56.patch and k22.patch to commit k23 alone.

